Notebook[{Cell["Lepton-quark scattering with transverse spin transfer, step 2 \
(FeynCalc route): spin and colour algebra", "Title"], 
  Cell["Input: Results/Amplitudes.wl from step 1 (the diagrams of l q -> q + \
X).  Output: Results/FeynCalc/Algebra.wl with the squared matrix elements of \
the Born, real-emission and photon-quark processes for the spin average \
(\"Unpolarized\") and for the transverse spin transfer (\"Transverse\"), and \
the virtual form factor family, in the same format as Processes/LeptonQuark \
so that step 3 is the same.\n\nThe observable.  The incoming quark k carries \
a transverse spin, the transverse spin of the observed quark p is measured, \
the lepton is unpolarized and the scattered lepton unobserved.  T denotes the \
full difference sigma(k up -> p up) - sigma(k up -> p down) at fixed incoming \
spin; by parity this is half the double difference, so T is obtained from the \
spin-averaged square by replacing the incoming density k-slash/2 by k-slash \
gamma5 a-slash/2 and the outgoing spin sum p-slash by p-slash gamma5 b-slash, \
where a and b are the unit transverse spin vectors of the two quarks (u ubar \
= p-slash (1 + gamma5 s-slash)/2 for a massless fermion).  Two directions are \
needed: the normal n to the scattering plane, the same for both quarks \
(T_NN), and the in-plane transverse directions aX, bX of the lepton-quark \
centre-of-mass frame (T_XX):\n\n   n: n.l = n.k = n.p = 0, n^2 = -1;   aX = \
(t/s) l + (u/s) k + p, orthogonal to l and k;   bX = t/(t+u) l - u/(t+u) k - \
s (u-t)/(t+u)^2 p, orthogonal to p and l + k,\n\nwith aX^2 = -t u/s and bX^2 \
= -s t u/(t+u)^2; T_XX is divided by the product of their lengths, -t \
u/(t+u), and the signs of the X axes are those of the paper (Section \
\"Observable and angular normalization\"): T_XX and T_NN coincide in four \
dimensions.  The Collins asymmetry needs the projection T_C = (T_XX + \
T_NN)/2, which is what is integrated (\"Transverse\"); the two components are \
kept separately in this file for inspection, since they differ by evanescent \
(D-4) terms.\n\nHVBM scheme.  The physical momenta l, k, p and the spin \
vectors are four-dimensional, the unobserved momenta lp and r of the real \
emission have (D-4)-dimensional parts with spe3 = rhat.rhat = lphat.lphat = \
-lphat.rhat, and gamma5 anticommutes with the four-dimensional gamma matrices \
only ($LeviCivitaSign = -1).  The real-emission tensor depends on the \
component nr = n.r of the unobserved gluon momentum along the normal; terms \
odd in nr vanish after the phase-space integration (they are odd under \
reflection of the scattering plane), and nr^2 is a rational function of the \
invariants: writing r = rpar + rn + rhat (parts in the plane of l, k, p, \
along n, and in the extra dimensions) and using r^2 = 0 gives nr^2 = rpar^2 + \
spe3 with rpar^2 = d.G^-1.d, G the Gram matrix of l, k, p and d = (l.r, k.r, \
p.r).\n\nConventions as in Processes/LeptonQuark: s = 2 l.k, t = -2 k.p, u = \
-2 l.p, a = (k-r)^2, b = (p+r)^2, tau = a + b + t, s4 = s + t + u; for the \
photon process sh = 2 q.k, th = -2 k.p, uh = -2 q.p.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Load", "Section"], Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["LoadFeynCalc[];\namplitudes = \
LoadAmplitudes[][\"FeynCalc\"];\nKeys[amplitudes]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Spin vectors and kinematics", "Section"], 
  Cell["The spin vectors are four-dimensional vectors of their own (nn, aX, \
bX) whose scalar products with every momentum are set from the definitions \
above: defineAxes[lIn, kIn, pOut, sIn, tIn, uIn, momenta] expands aX.x and \
bX.x for the listed momenta x through the scalar products of lIn, kIn, pOut \
already in force, so that the same definitions serve the photon process (with \
the photon momentum q in place of l).", "Text"], 
  Cell["FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"BMHV\"];\n$LeviCivitaSign = \
-1;\ncouplingNames = {SMP[\"e\"] -> ee, SMP[\"g_s\"] -> \
gs};\nnormalProducts[momenta_List] := (SPD[nn] = -1; SP[nn] = -1; \
Scan[(SPD[nn, #] = 0; SP[nn, #] = 0) &, momenta]; Momentum[nn, D - 4] = \
0);\ndefineAxes[lIn_, kIn_, pOut_, sIn_, tIn_, uIn_, momenta_List] := \
Module[{base = {lIn, kIn, pOut}, ca, cb, product},\n  ca = {tIn/sIn, uIn/sIn, \
1};                                                        (* aX = (t/s) l + \
(u/s) k + p *)\n  cb = {tIn/(tIn + uIn), -uIn/(tIn + uIn), -sIn (uIn - \
tIn)/(tIn + uIn)^2};         (* bX = t/(t+u) l - u/(t+u) k - s (u-t)/(t+u)^2 \
p *)\n  product[c1_, c2_] := Factor[Sum[c1[[i]] c2[[j]] SP[base[[i]], \
base[[j]]], {i, 3}, {j, 3}]];\n  Scan[(Momentum[#, D - 4] = 0) &, {aX, \
bX}];\n  Do[SP[aX, x] = SPD[aX, x] = Factor[Sum[ca[[i]] SP[base[[i]], x], {i, \
3}]];\n     SP[bX, x] = SPD[bX, x] = Factor[Sum[cb[[i]] SP[base[[i]], x], {i, \
3}]], {x, momenta}];\n  SP[aX, nn] = SPD[aX, nn] = 0; SP[bX, nn] = SPD[bX, \
nn] = 0;\n  SP[aX] = SPD[aX] = product[ca, ca]; SP[bX] = SPD[bX] = \
product[cb, cb]; SP[aX, bX] = SPD[aX, bX] = product[ca, cb];\n  <|\"aX\" -> \
aX, \"bX\" -> bX, \"Lengths\" -> -tIn uIn/(tIn + uIn)|>];\nbornKinematics := \
(FCClearScalarProducts[];\n  SetMandelstam[s, t, u, l, k, -lp, -p, 0, 0, 0, \
0];\n  Scan[(Momentum[#, D - 4] = 0) &, {l, k, lp, p}];\n  normalProducts[{l, \
k, p, lp}]);\nrealKinematics := (FCClearScalarProducts[];\n  \
Scan[(Momentum[#, D - 4] = 0) &, {l, k, p, pRec}];\n  SPD[l] = 0; SPD[k] = 0; \
SPD[lp] = 0; SPD[p] = 0; SPD[r] = 0;\n  SPD[l, k] = s/2; SPD[k, p] = -t/2; \
SPD[l, p] = -u/2; SPD[k, r] = -a/2; SPD[p, r] = b/2;\n  SPD[l, lp] = -(a + b \
+ t)/2; SPD[l, r] = (s + t + u + a + b)/2; SPD[k, lp] = (s + t + a)/2;\n  \
SPD[lp, p] = -(t + u + b)/2; SPD[lp, r] = (s + t + u)/2;\n  SPE[lp] = spe3; \
SPE[r] = spe3; SPE[lp, r] = -spe3;\n  SP[l] = 0; SP[k] = 0; SP[p] = 0; SP[lp] \
= -spe3; SP[r] = -spe3;\n  SP[l, k] = s/2; SP[k, p] = -t/2; SP[l, p] = -u/2; \
SP[k, r] = -a/2; SP[p, r] = b/2;\n  SP[l, lp] = -(a + b + t)/2; SP[l, r] = (s \
+ t + u + a + b)/2; SP[k, lp] = (s + t + a)/2;\n  SP[lp, p] = -(t + u + b)/2; \
SP[lp, r] = (s + t + u)/2 + spe3;\n  normalProducts[{l, k, p}]; SPD[nn, r] = \
nr; SP[nn, r] = nr; SPD[nn, lp] = -nr; SP[nn, lp] = -nr);\nphotonKinematics \
:= (FCClearScalarProducts[];\n  Scan[(Momentum[#, D - 4] = 0) &, {q, k, p, \
r}];\n  SPD[q] = 0; SPD[k] = 0; SPD[p] = 0; SPD[r] = 0;\n  SPD[q, k] = sh/2; \
SPD[k, p] = -th/2; SPD[q, p] = -uh/2; SPD[p, r] = sh/2; SPD[k, r] = -uh/2; \
SPD[q, r] = -th/2;\n  SP[q] = 0; SP[k] = 0; SP[p] = 0; SP[r] = 0;\n  SP[q, k] \
= sh/2; SP[k, p] = -th/2; SP[q, p] = -uh/2; SP[p, r] = sh/2; SP[k, r] = \
-uh/2; SP[q, r] = -th/2;\n  normalProducts[{q, k, p, \
r}]);\nbornKinematics;\nbornAxes = defineAxes[l, k, p, s, t, u, {l, k, p, \
lp}];\nRequire[Simplify[{SP[aX, l], SP[aX, k], SP[bX, p], SP[bX, l] + SP[bX, \
k], SP[aX] + t u/s, SP[bX] + s t u/(t + u)^2} /. u -> -s - t] === {0, 0, 0, \
0, 0, 0},\n  \"The in-plane axes are not what the text says\"];\n{SP[aX], \
SP[bX], SP[aX, bX]}", "Input"], Cell["Squares from explicit traces", 
   "Section"], Cell["For each process the lepton trace Tr[lp-slash gamma^mu \
l-slash gamma^nu]/2 (or, for the photon process, the photon polarization sum) \
multiplies the quark trace Tr[rho_out W_i rho_in W-bar_j], where W_i are the \
strings of the diagrams, rho_in = k-slash/2 (average) or k-slash gamma5 \
a-slash/2 and rho_out = p-slash (sum) or p-slash gamma5 b-slash.  spinCase is \
\"Unpolarized\", \"NN\" or \"XX\".  The strings (photon index mu, gluon index \
rho, all D-dimensional):\n\n  Born:   W = gamma^mu / t;\n  Real:   W_1 = \
gamma^mu (k-slash - r-slash) gamma^rho / a,   W_2 = gamma^rho (p-slash + \
r-slash) gamma^mu / b,   times 1/tau^2, gluon sum -g;\n  Photon: W_1 = \
gamma^rho (k-slash + q-slash) gamma^mu / sh,   W_2 = gamma^mu (k-slash - \
r-slash) gamma^rho / uh,   photon sum -g/(D-2), gluon sum -g.\n\nColour CF = \
Tr[T^a T^a]/Nc (Born: 1).  As in Processes/LeptonOffDiagonal, the unpolarized \
case built from the same strings is checked against FeynCalc's generic spin \
sum, and the amplitude records of step 1 show that the strings are those of \
the diagrams.", "Text"], Cell["reverse[string_] := (string /. {mu -> nu, rho \
-> sigma}) /. Dot -> (Dot @@ Reverse[{##}] &);\nsimplifyTrace[expr_] := \
Factor[Together[Simplify[Contract[ExpandScalarProduct[Contract[DiracSimplify[\
expr, DiracTraceEvaluate -> True]]]]]]];\ndensity[spinCase_, aIn_, bOut_] := \
Switch[spinCase,\n  \"Unpolarized\", {GS[k]/2, GS[p]},\n  \"NN\", \
{GS[k].GA[5].GS[nn]/2, GS[p].GA[5].GS[nn]},\n  \"XX\", \
{GS[k].GA[5].GS[aIn]/2, GS[p].GA[5].GS[bOut]}];\nleptonTrace = \
DiracTrace[GSD[lp].GAD[mu].GSD[l].GAD[nu]]/2;\nquarkTrace[strings_, \
spinCase_, ax_] := With[{rho = density[spinCase, ax[\"aX\"], ax[\"bX\"]]},\n  \
Table[DiracTrace[rho[[2]].strings[[i]].rho[[1]].reverse[strings[[j]]]], {i, \
Length[strings]}, {j, Length[strings]}]];\nlengths[spinCase_, ax_] := \
If[spinCase === \"XX\", ax[\"Lengths\"], 1];", "Input"], 
  Cell["Born: l q -> l q", "Section"], Cell["Expected: the unpolarized square \
2 ee^4 eq^2 ((s^2 + u^2)/t^2 - eps) as in the lepton-quark process, and the \
transverse tensors ee^4 eq^2 [-4 s u/t^2 -+ (D-4)] (Eq. \
(transverse-born-tensor) of the paper): equal in four dimensions, with \
opposite evanescent terms, so that the Collins projection has none.", 
   "Text"], Cell["bornKinematics; bornAxes = defineAxes[l, k, p, s, t, u, {l, \
k, p, lp}];\nbornGeneric = Module[{amp = Total[amplitudes[\"Born\"]]},\n  amp \
ComplexConjugate[amp]/SUNN // FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit // SUNSimplify[#, \
Explicit -> True] & //\n    FermionSpinSum[#, ExtraFactor -> 1/4] & // \
DiracSimplify[#, DiracTraceEvaluate -> True] & // Contract //\n    \
TrickMandelstam[#, {s, t, u, 0}] & // Factor // ReplaceAll[#, couplingNames] \
&];\nbornByTraces[spinCase_] := ee^4 eq^2/lengths[spinCase, bornAxes] \
TrickMandelstam[Factor[Together[\n  Total[simplifyTrace[leptonTrace #] & /@ \
Flatten[quarkTrace[{GAD[mu]/t}, spinCase, bornAxes]]]]], {s, t, u, \
0}];\nRequire[Simplify[bornByTraces[\"Unpolarized\"] - bornGeneric] === 0, \
\"The explicit traces do not reproduce the unpolarized Born square\"];\nborn \
= <|\"Unpolarized\" -> bornGeneric, \"NN\" -> bornByTraces[\"NN\"], \"XX\" -> \
bornByTraces[\"XX\"]|>;\nborn[\"Transverse\"] = Factor[(born[\"NN\"] + \
born[\"XX\"])/2];\nRequire[Simplify[(born[\"Unpolarized\"] - 2 ee^4 eq^2 \
((s^2 + u^2)/t^2 - (4 - D)/2)) /. u -> -s - t] === 0, \"Born square differs \
from the textbook result\"];\nRequire[Simplify[{born[\"NN\"] - ee^4 eq^2 (-4 \
s u/t^2 - (D - 4)), born[\"XX\"] - ee^4 eq^2 (-4 s u/t^2 + (D - 4))} /. u -> \
-s - t] === {0, 0},\n  \"Transverse Born tensors differ from Eq. \
(transverse-born-tensor) of the paper\"];\nborn", "Input"], 
  Cell["Virtual: the one-loop vertex correction", "Section"], 
  Cell["The vertex graph gives a vector form factor times the Born current \
(the massless on-shell vertex has no other structure, see \
Processes/LeptonQuark), so the interference 2 Re(M_vertex M_Born^ is the same \
multiple of the Born square for every spin projection.  The scalar family \
VirtualIntegral[n0,n1,n2] is extracted exactly as in the lepton-quark \
process.", "Text"], Cell["FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"NDR\"];\nFCClearScalarProdu\
cts[];\nSetMandelstam[s, t, u, l, k, -lp, -p, 0, 0, 0, \
0];\n$KeepLogDivergentScalelessIntegrals = True;\nbornAmplitude = \
Total[amplitudes[\"Born\"]];\nvertexAmplitude = \
Total[amplitudes[\"VirtualVertex\"]] // DiracSimplify // Contract // \
SUNSimplify[#, SUNNToCACF -> True] &;\nvertexScalar = vertexAmplitude // \
TID[#, loop, ToPaVe -> True] & // DiracSimplify // Contract //\n  \
SUNSimplify[#, SUNNToCACF -> True] & // \
FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit;\nbornReduced = bornAmplitude // DiracSimplify // \
Contract // FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit;\nsquare[x_, y_] := x \
ComplexConjugate[y] // FermionSpinSum[#, ExtraFactor -> 1/4] & // \
DiracSimplify //\n  SUNSimplify[#, SUNNToCACF -> True] & // \
TrickMandelstam[#, {s, t, u, 0}] & // Simplify;\nvirtualRatio = \
Factor[square[2 vertexScalar, bornReduced]/square[bornReduced, \
bornReduced]];\nvirtualFamily = Factor[virtualRatio/(2 CF Pi^2 \
SMP[\"g_s\"]^2)] /. {\n  B0[0, 0, 0] -> VirtualIntegral[1, 1, 0], B0[t, 0, 0] \
-> VirtualIntegral[0, 1, 1],\n  C0[0, 0, t, 0, 0, 0] -> VirtualIntegral[1, 1, \
1]}", "Input"], Cell["Real emission: l q -> l q g", "Section"], 
  Cell["The tensors are polynomials in nr; the odd part is dropped (it \
integrates to zero) after checking that it is at most linear, and nr^2 is \
replaced as explained above.  The unpolarized square is also computed with \
FeynCalc's generic tools and compared.", "Text"], 
  Cell["FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"BMHV\"];\nrealKinematics;\nrealAxes = \
defineAxes[l, k, p, s, t, u, {l, k, p, lp, r}];\nrealStrings = \
{GAD[mu].(GSD[k] - GSD[r]).GAD[rho]/a, GAD[rho].(GSD[p] + \
GSD[r]).GAD[mu]/b};\nrealByTraces[spinCase_] := CF ee^4 eq^2 gs^2/((a + b + \
t)^2 lengths[spinCase, realAxes]) Factor[Together[\n  \
Total[simplifyTrace[leptonTrace # (-MTD[rho, sigma])] & /@ \
Flatten[quarkTrace[realStrings, spinCase, realAxes]]]]];\ngram = Table[SP[x, \
y], {x, {l, k, p}}, {y, {l, k, p}}];\nparallelSquare = Factor[{SP[l, r], \
SP[k, r], SP[p, r]}.Inverse[gram].{SP[l, r], SP[k, r], SP[p, r]}];       (* \
rpar^2 *)\nnormalReduction[expr_] := Module[{coefficients = \
CoefficientList[Expand[expr], nr]},\n  Require[Length[coefficients] <= 3, \
\"The real-emission tensor has a power of nr above two\", \
Length[coefficients] - 1];\n  Factor[coefficients[[1]] + \
If[Length[coefficients] == 3, coefficients[[3]] (parallelSquare + spe3), \
0]]];\nrealUnpolarized = Module[{amp = Total[SUNSimplify[#, SUNNToCACF -> \
True] & /@ amplitudes[\"Real\"]] // DiracSimplify // Contract},\n  amp \
ComplexConjugate[amp]/SUNN // FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit // SUNSimplify[#, \
Explicit -> True, SUNNToCACF -> True] & //\n    FermionSpinSum[#, ExtraFactor \
-> 1/4] & // DiracSimplify // Contract // DoPolarizationSums[#, r, 0, \
VirtualBoson -> True] & //\n    Contract // Simplify // SUNSimplify[#, \
SUNNToCACF -> True] & // Factor // ReplaceAll[#, couplingNames] \
&];\nRequire[Together[(realByTraces[\"Unpolarized\"] /. spe3 -> 0) - \
realUnpolarized] === 0, \"The explicit traces do not reproduce the \
unpolarized real square\"];\nreal = <|\"Unpolarized\" -> realUnpolarized, \
\"NN\" -> normalReduction[realByTraces[\"NN\"]], \"XX\" -> \
normalReduction[realByTraces[\"XX\"]]|>;\nreal[\"Transverse\"] = \
Factor[(real[\"NN\"] + real[\"XX\"])/2];\nRequire[FreeQ[real, nr | nn], \"The \
normal component was not eliminated\"];\n{parallelSquare, \
Factor[(real[\"NN\"] - real[\"XX\"]) /. {D -> 4, spe3 -> 0}]}", "Input"], 
  Cell["In four dimensions and without the hatted terms the two transverse \
components coincide (displayed above: zero), as for the Born tensor.", 
   "Text"], Cell["Require[Factor[(real[\"NN\"] - real[\"XX\"]) /. {D -> 4, \
spe3 -> 0}] === 0, \"The two transverse components differ in four \
dimensions\"];\nFactor[real[\"Transverse\"] /. {D -> 4, spe3 -> 0}]", 
   "Input"], Cell["Photon-quark Born: gamma q -> q g", "Section"], 
  Cell["Needed through order eps for the photon-in-lepton subtraction (the \
photon is unpolarized).  Axes as above with the photon momentum q in place of \
l.  Expected transverse projection (Eq. (transverse-photon-born) of the \
paper, CF ee^2 eq^2 gs^2 removed): 4 - 2 eps^2 th^2/((1-eps) sh uh).", 
   "Text"], Cell["photonKinematics;\nphotonAxes = defineAxes[q, k, p, sh, th, \
uh, {q, k, p, r}];\nphotonStrings = {GAD[rho].(GSD[k] + GSD[q]).GAD[mu]/sh, \
GAD[mu].(GSD[k] - GSD[r]).GAD[rho]/uh};\nphotonByTraces[spinCase_] := CF ee^2 \
eq^2 gs^2/lengths[spinCase, photonAxes] \
Factor[TrickMandelstam[Cancel[Together[\n  Total[simplifyTrace[(-MTD[mu, \
nu]/(D - 2)) # (-MTD[rho, sigma])] & /@ Flatten[quarkTrace[photonStrings, \
spinCase, photonAxes]]]]], {sh, th, uh, 0}]];\nphotonGeneric = Module[{amp = \
Total[SUNSimplify[#, SUNNToCACF -> True] & /@ amplitudes[\"Photon\"]] // \
DiracSimplify // Contract, expr},\n  expr = amp ComplexConjugate[amp]/SUNN // \
FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit // SUNSimplify[#, Explicit -> True, SUNNToCACF -> \
True] & //\n    FermionSpinSum[#, ExtraFactor -> 1/2] & // DiracSimplify // \
Contract // DoPolarizationSums[#, r, 0, VirtualBoson -> True] & //\n    \
DoPolarizationSums[#, q, 0, VirtualBoson -> True] & // Contract // Simplify \
// SUNSimplify[#, SUNNToCACF -> True] & // Factor;\n  TrickMandelstam[expr/(D \
- 2), {sh, th, uh, 0}] /. \
couplingNames];\nRequire[Simplify[(photonByTraces[\"Unpolarized\"] - \
photonGeneric) /. uh -> -sh - th] === 0, \"The explicit traces do not \
reproduce the unpolarized photon square\"];\nphoton = <|\"Unpolarized\" -> \
photonGeneric, \"NN\" -> photonByTraces[\"NN\"], \"XX\" -> \
photonByTraces[\"XX\"]|>;\nphoton[\"Transverse\"] = \
Factor[TrickMandelstam[(photon[\"NN\"] + photon[\"XX\"])/2, {sh, th, uh, \
0}]];\nRequire[Simplify[(photon[\"Transverse\"]/(CF ee^2 eq^2 gs^2) - (4 - 2 \
eps^2 th^2/((1 - eps) sh uh))) /. D -> 4 - 2 eps /. uh -> -sh - th] === 0,\n  \
\"The photon transverse tensor differs from Eq. (transverse-photon-born) of \
the paper\"];\nphoton", "Input"], Cell["Save", "Section"], 
  Cell["Algebra.wl holds everything step 3 needs, in the format of the \
lepton-quark process: the squares with the keys \"Unpolarized\" and \
\"Transverse\" (and the two components \"NN\", \"XX\" for inspection) and the \
virtual family.", "Text"], Cell["algebra = <|\"Born\" -> born, \"Real\" -> \
real, \"Photon\" -> photon, \"VirtualFamily\" -> \
virtualFamily|>;\nSaveResult[\"Algebra\", algebra, \
\"FeynCalc\"];\nKeys[algebra]", "Input"]}, WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
